hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"147","It is narrated by Muhammad bin Abi Safwan Al-Thaqafi, it is narrated by Abdul Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, it is narrated by Zaida bin Qudamah, on the authority of Khalid bin Alqamah Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Abd Khair, who said: Ali entered al-Rahba after the dawn prayer, then he said to a boy of his: Bring me something to purify, so the boy came to him. With a vessel containing water and a basin, Abdul Khair said as we sat looking at him, “So he took the vessel with his right hand, and placed it on his left hand, then washed His palms, then he took the vessel with his right hand and emptied it into his left hand. He did it three times.” Abdul Khair said: All of this without his hand inserting the vessel. Until he washed it several times, then he put his right hand into the vessel and filled his mouth. He rinsed his mouth and sniffed it, and sprinkled it with his left hand three times, then washed it. His face three times, then he washed his right hand three times up to the elbow, then he washed his left hand three times up to the elbow, then he inserted his hand He placed the right hand in the vessel until the water submerged it, then he raised it with the amount of water it carried, then he wiped it with his left hand, then he wiped his head with both hands. Or all of them, then he inserted his right hand into the vessel, then poured water on his right foot, washed it three times with his left hand, then poured it with his hand. He placed his right foot over his left foot, then washed it three times with his left hand, then he inserted his right hand and filled it with water, then drank from it. Then he said: The purification of the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So whoever likes to look at the purity of the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, this is his purification."
